   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Eval/Sign.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the lemma and the file; at use sites the canonical post-PR API is `eval_map_apply` (simp) followed by `hf.sign_comp`. If a named lemma is kept for the roadmap's real-closure work, give it a statement whose LHS survives simp and that a consumer actually needs (e.g. the zero/positivity transfer `(p.map f).eval (f x) = 0 \u2194 p.eval x = 0` and `0 < (p.map f).eval (f x) \u2194 0 < p.eval x`), rather than restating the two-lemma composite.",
   "issue": "`Polynomial.sign_eval_map`'s LHS `sign ((p.map f).eval (f x))` is not in simp normal form: `Polynomial.eval_map_apply` is `@[simp]` and rewrites the inner subterm to `f (p.eval x)`, leaving `sign (f (p.eval x))`, which this lemma no longer matches. The exported name therefore cannot be annotated `@[simp]` (it would never fire) and silently fails to apply in any goal `simp` has touched \u2014 exactly where the residual goal is closed by Mathlib's `StrictMono.sign_comp`, which is the entire proof body.",
   "line": "23"
  }
